--- A row written into a matrix holds the matrix's own length: where the
--- lengths are known before the program runs, a row of another length is
--- refused (tests/errors i06); where one is known only as the program
--- runs — a list grown by push, handed to a function — the write stops
--- there, in the same words in both modes.
use math
fn put[t, row]
    t[0] = row
    return t
ok = push[push[[], 1.0], 2.0]
log[put[zeros[2, 2], ok]]
long = push[ok, 3.0]
log[put[zeros[2, 2], long]]
log['not reached']
